# Your bat options: ~/.config/kubaos/tools/bat/config, appended to KubaOS's, so they win.
# dot-config apply, which every update runs, writes ~/.config/bat/config from both: run
# it after editing. bat also colours the fzf preview and delta's diffs.
#
# The colours: "base16" (KubaOS) follows the terminal's, which follow the wallpaper.
# `bat --list-themes` lists the rest.
# --theme=base16
#
# What frames the text (KubaOS: numbers,changes,header-filename); "plain" for none.
# --style=numbers,changes,header-filename
#
# Tab width in spaces (bat's default, 4).
# --tabs=4
#
# Long lines: "auto" (bat's default) wraps them, "never" cuts them.
# --wrap=auto
#
# Full docs: man bat (https://github.com/sharkdp/bat#configuration-file).
